    "https://slu.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/SLU-Saint-Louis-MO/Administrative-Assistant-II---Center-for-Advanced-Dental-Education_2026-10104": {
      "title": "Administrative Assistant II , Center for Advanced Dental Education",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-14\nFull time\n\nWho is Saint Louis University? Founded in 1818, Saint Louis University is one of the nation’s oldest and most prestigious Catholic universities. SLU, which also has a campus in Madrid, Spain, is recognized for world-class academics, life-changing research, compassionate health care, and a strong commitment to faith and service. The Administrative Assistant II provides administrative and operational support for the Center for Advanced Dental Education (CADE), including coordination of academic program support, student/resident records, course and curriculum updates, event planning, financial processing, and day-to-day office operations. PRIMARY JOB RESPONSIBILITIES Provides administrative support for CADE’s day-to-day operations, including working with residents, faculty, staff, student workers, and campus partners to coordinate academic, operational, and office support needs Maintains and updates academic and program information, including course catalog details, class updates, curriculum-related records, Canvas information, SLATE records, and grade entry support Coordinates graduation ceremonies and department events, including two graduations annually in June and December, the CADE picnic, CPR classes, meetings, and other program activities Processes and tracks financial and administrative items such as reimbursements, Workday Finance transactions, service requests, supplies, and related documentation Serves as a liaison with housekeeping, facilities, and other university departments to submit, coordinate, and follow up on service requests and operational needs Supervises approximately three to four student workers, assigning support tasks related to office operations, event setup, and event support Answers and responds to emails, phone calls, and inquiries regarding department programs, academic processes, events, and operational requests; communicates information clearly and professionally Handles confidential or sensitive student, resident, academic, and departmental records with discretion and accuracy Performs other duties as assigned KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS, AND ABILITIES Knowledge of university academic, administrative, and student support processes Ability to support residents, faculty, staff, and students with professionalism, responsiveness, and sound judgment Strong organizational, time management, and follow-through skills Verbal and written communication skills Ability to maintain accurate records, enter grades, update databases, and manage academic or program information with attention to detail Proficiency with Microsoft Office and Excel  Experience with Workday, SLATE and/or Canvas is a plus Ability to coordinate events, manage logistics, and work with campus partners Ability to supervise and direct the work of student staff Ability to handle multiple priorities, meet deadlines, and remain available and responsive during regular business hours Ability to maintain confidentiality MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS High School Diploma and three years of administrative support, academic support, clerical, or related work experience PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS Associate's degree Experience working in a university or academic environment; familiarity with SLU systems, academic processes, resident or student support, event coordination, Workday, SLATE, Canvas, and Microsoft Office preferred. Function Administrative Support/ Cross-functional Family Scheduled Weekly Hours: 40 Saint Louis University is an equal opportunity/affirmative action employer. All qualified candidates will receive consideration for the position applied for without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, disability, marital status, sexual orientation, military/veteran status, gender identity, or other non-merit factors. If accommodations are needed for completing the application and/or with the interviewing process, please contact Human Resources at 314-977-5847."
    },
    "https://slu.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/SLU-Saint-Louis-MO/Admission-Counselor-I_2026-09998": {
      "title": "Admission Counselor I",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-14\nFull time\n\nWho is Saint Louis University? Founded in 1818, Saint Louis University is one of the nation’s oldest and most prestigious Catholic universities. SLU, which also has a campus in Madrid, Spain, is recognized for world-class academics, life-changing research, compassionate health care, and a strong commitment to faith and service. JOB SUMMARY The Admission Counselor I role at Saint Louis University supports the institution’s enrollment goals by engaging with prospective students and their families throughout the admissions process. This position is responsible to identify, recruit, admit, and enroll academically qualified traditional or non-traditional students in accordance with the philosophy of the University. This position involves recruitment travel, application review, event planning, and counseling students on the admissions process, academic offerings, and campus life. PRIMARY JOB RESPONSIBILITIES Establishes and maintains an informational, active communication system with either traditional high school or college students, parents and counselors, or post-traditional degree-seeking adults Counsels student applicants concerning admission, financial aid, career planning, and housing options; explains, interprets, and provides outreach to students regarding the FAFSA and financial aid awards Identifies, recruits, and enrolls prospective students in a designated market; manages a recruitment territory; develops recruitment strategies Plans and arranges all phases of regional and local travel; conducts office-based contact by mail and phone with students, and parents if applicable; may make reservations Reads, interprets, and evaluates students’ academic credentials and makes admission/denial decisions; assists with scholarship appropriation Participates as an active member of the recruitment team; assists with special programs and research projects; participates in the development and implementation of enrollment strategies Perform various administrative tasks, to include composing routine letters, compiling data for reports, maintaining calendars, processing applications, scheduling appointments, maintains confidential files, prepares position papers/reports, inputs/retrieves data on information system software, etc. Performs other duties as assigned KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS, AND ABILITIES Interpersonal/human relations skills Verbal and written communication skills Effective presentation skills Planning and organizational skills Basic research skills Ability to operate personal computer with various software programs Ability to learn and apply institutional policies and procedures Ability to maintain schedules Ability to demonstrate self-direction and motivation Ability to work effectively in a team setting Ability to travel/drive and work on weekends and nights Ability to handle stress due to travel  Ability to multi-task and deal with competing priorities Ability to build relationships with and recruit a diverse population of students in all parts of the United States Ability to maintain confidential information   MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS Bachelor's degree Applicants must have a valid driver's license and maintain active personal car insurance throughout the duration of employment Ability to rent a car, fly, ability to book a hotel for overnight travel, and ability to travel locally Applicants must include: 1) a cover letter; 2) a resume/curriculum vitae.  You can upload these items on the third page \"My experience\" of the application Salary/Benefits: Salary for Admission Counselor I ($47,500), plus benefits including vacation and sick leave, health/dental/vision/life insurance, 403B retirement savings plan and match, tuition remission benefits , employee assistance program and wellness program. Function Admissions Scheduled Weekly Hours: 40 Saint Louis University is an equal opportunity/affirmative action employer. All qualified candidates will receive consideration for the position applied for without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, disability, marital status, sexual orientation, military/veteran status, gender identity, or other non-merit factors. If accommodations are needed for completing the application and/or with the interviewing process, please contact Human Resources at 314-977-5847."
