    "https://slu.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/SLU-Saint-Louis-MO/Manager--Administrative-Support-Services_2026-10079-1": {
      "title": "Manager, Administrative Support Services",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-12\nFull time\n\nWho is Saint Louis University? Founded in 1818, Saint Louis University is one of the nation’s oldest and most prestigious Catholic universities. SLU, which also has a campus in Madrid, Spain, is recognized for world-class academics, life-changing research, compassionate health care, and a strong commitment to faith and service. JOB SUMMARY The Manager of Administrative Support Services provides leadership and oversight for administrative operations and support staff. This role ensures consistent, high-quality administrative services, effective workload and resource management, and a strong service-oriented culture in support of academic leadership, faculty, students, and external stakeholders. The position emphasizes people leadership, process improvement, and operational effectiveness while ensuring compliance with university policies, accreditation standards, and regulatory requirements unique to education.   PRIMARY JOB RESPONSIBILITIES Staff Leadership & Supervision Directly supervises, coaches, and develops a team of administrative support staff, which may include administrative assistants, program support staff, and student workers Establishes clear performance expectations; conducts regular performance evaluations; and addresses performance issues in a timely, constructive manner Builds staffing schedules, assigns work, and balances workloads to ensure continuity of operations and coverage during absences Supports talent management activities, including hiring, onboarding, training, cross-training, and staff engagement initiatives Fosters a collaborative, inclusive, and service-driven work environment Administrative Operations & Service Delivery Oversees day-to-day administrative support operations for a school/department, ensuring timely, accurate, and professional service delivery Partners with school academic departments, clinics, and administrative units to ensure administrative needs are met consistently Standardizes processes, templates, and service expectations across administrative functions to improve efficiency and reduce variability Serves as a point of escalation for complex or sensitive administrative issues requiring judgment, discretion, or cross-unit coordination Financial, Resource, and Academic Support Assists Business Director and Department Chairs with management of department budgets, including monitoring expenditures and preparing reports Oversees purchasing and expense processes in compliance with university and regulatory requirements Supports faculty and academic administration, including scheduling coordination, program support, and reporting obligations Assists with logistics and administrative support for school events, meetings, clinics, and special programs Process Improvement & Compliance Identifies opportunities to improve workflows, reduces manual processes, and enhances service delivery through standardization and effective system use Ensures administrative practices comply with university policies, confidentiality requirements, and records-management expectations Supports compliance with HR and financial processes by ensuring staff follow approved procedures and timelines ​Communication & Collaboration Acts as a liaison between administrative support staff and school leadership to ensure clear communication of priorities, expectations, and changes Partners with central administrative offices (e.g., Registrar, Facilities, IT) to resolve issues and coordinate services Promotes a collaborative service culture that supports faculty effectiveness and student success Strategic Initiatives & Special Projects Leads or contributes to special projects, strategic initiatives, and operational improvements as assigned by school leadership Performs other duties as assigned   KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS, AND ABILITIES Strong organizational, interpersonal, and communication skills Strong analytical and problem-solving skills Proven ability to exercise sound judgment and discretion Ability to lead, coach, and motivate staff in a service-driven environment Ability to manage competing priorities and adapt to changing demands High level of professionalism and commitment to continuous improvement   MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS Bachelor’s degree Three (3) or more years of experience supervising or leading administrative or professional staff Demonstrated experience managing complex administrative operations in an academic or professional services environment Ability to regularly travel between six North Campus buildings to provide effective staff oversight and support   PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS Master’s degree Experience in higher education Applicants must include: 1) a cover letter; 2) a resume/curriculum vitae; You can upload these items on the third page \"My experience\" of the application. BENEFITS: Saint Louis University offers excellent full-time benefits including vacation and sick leave, health/dental/vision/life insurance, 403B retirement savings plan and match, tuition remission , employee assistance program, and wellness program. WORK SCHEDULE EXPECTATIONS: This is a fully in-person position and will require the individual to work at Macelwane Hall with the College of Arts and Sciences on campus at Saint Louis University. Function Administrative Support/ Cross-functional Family Scheduled Weekly Hours: 40 Saint Louis University is an equal opportunity/affirmative action employer. All qualified candidates will receive consideration for the position applied for without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, disability, marital status, sexual orientation, military/veteran status, gender identity, or other non-merit factors. If accommodations are needed for completing the application and/or with the interviewing process, please contact Human Resources at 314-977-5847."
    },
    "https://slu.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/SLU-Saint-Louis-MO/Operations-Coordinator--Workforce-Center-_2026-10119": {
      "title": "Operations Coordinator (Workforce Center)",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-08\nFull time\n\nWho is Saint Louis University? Founded in 1818, Saint Louis University is one of the nation’s oldest and most prestigious Catholic universities. SLU, which also has a campus in Madrid, Spain, is recognized for world-class academics, life-changing research, compassionate health care, and a strong commitment to faith and service. JOB SUMMARY The Operations Coordinator provides tactical planning and support for the Workforce Center. This position ensures a high quality training environment for all clients, and assists with managing relationships with outside clients and vendors, including large employers, training vendors, academic partners and test vendors. PRIMARY JOB RESPONSIBILITIES Evaluates and improves Workforce Center operations to support revenue goals and growth initiatives; makes adjustments as needed to enhance performance Manages supply vendors and supports access to technology resources Works closely with external clients, vendors, students, training partners, instructors, and the sales team Provides administrative and operational support for training delivery, including preparation of materials and coordination of logistical details to ensure courses are set up for success; works in close collaboration with leadership and the training partner to align course operations with strategic goals and program standards; supports communication with instructors and vendors as needed, ensuring timely execution of training activities Leads the operational implementation of student services and acts as a point of contact for external clients across communication platforms; provides direct support to students throughout their learning experience—from initial inquiry and registration to accessing virtual classes, completing course evaluations, and receiving certificates of completion and digital badges Continuously updates operational procedures to enhance the student and client experience Generates and maintains operational reports related to course enrollments, revenue tracking, and cost monitoring; manages purchasing card (P-Card) reconciliation, prepares client invoices, and oversees collections to ensure timely and accurate financial processing Performs other duties as assigned KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS, AND ABILITIES Proficient in Microsoft Office Suite, Google Docs, Salesforce and Adobe Acrobat Strong interpersonal skills Strong verbal and written communication skills Excellent customer service orientation and client engagement abilities Strong problem solving skills Exceptional attention to detail with strong organizational and time management skills Positive team player with the ability to take direction and complete tasks efficiently Ability to quickly learn new software platforms, including online registration and evaluation systems MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS High School Diploma or the equivalent Three or more years of relevant professional experience PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS Bachelor's degree ABOUT THE TEAM The Workforce Center was established in 2013 to address the skill needs of our modern and fast-paced workplaces. Powered by top-ranked Saint Louis University, the Workforce Center provides premier training solutions to corporations and individuals nationwide. With a mission to fulfill the needs of modern organizations, the Center offers a range of training topics including Cyber Security, Project Management, Agile, Analytics, Software Engineering and more. Learn more about the Workforce Center at SLU. Function Staff Program Support Scheduled Weekly Hours: 40 Saint Louis University is an equal opportunity/affirmative action employer. All qualified candidates will receive consideration for the position applied for without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, disability, marital status, sexual orientation, military/veteran status, gender identity, or other non-merit factors. If accommodations are needed for completing the application and/or with the interviewing process, please contact Human Resources at 314-977-5847."
    },
    "https://slu.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/Doisy-Research-Center/Post-Doctoral-Fellow-for-Research-Lab_2026-10108": {
      "title": "Post Doctoral Fellow for Research Lab",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-07\nFull time\n\nWho is Saint Louis University? Founded in 1818, Saint Louis University is one of the nation’s oldest and most prestigious Catholic universities. SLU, which also has a campus in Madrid, Spain, is recognized for world-class academics, life-changing research, compassionate health care, and a strong commitment to faith and service. A postdoctoral fellow research position is available, focused on pediatric intestinal failure, short bowel syndrome, parenteral nutrition associated injury, bile acid signaling, microbiome related mechanisms, epithelial biology,  liver injury and other systemic processes and diseases. The successful candidate will join a multidisciplinary team studying how intestinal nutrient exposure, microbial metabolites, epithelial signaling, and gut and liver communication regulate intestinal adaptation, barrier function, inflammation, liver disease and other systemic processes and diseases.  The postdoctoral fellow will work across complementary experimental systems, including neonatal large animal models, intestinal epithelial organoid-derived cultures, liver organoid or liver-derived cell systems, human tissue-based studies, molecular and multi-omic assays and others.  Responsibilities The postdoctoral fellow will participate in experimental planning, execution, data analysis, and interpretation. Responsibilities may include large animal sample collection and processing, epithelial organoid culture and functional assays, liver organoid or liver-derived cell assays, molecular biology, immunostaining, imaging, quantitative PCR, ELISA or multiplex assays, microbiome and metabolomic sample preparation, bile acid and short chain fatty acid related analyses, and integration of physiologic, histologic, molecular,  omics datasets and tasks as required by the lab. The post-doc will be expected to maintain accurate laboratory records, contribute to protocol development and quality control, prepare figures and manuscripts, present findings at laboratory meetings and scientific conferences, and assist with grant progress reports and future grant applications. The position requires close collaboration with investigators in pediatric gastroenterology, hepatology, pathology, microbiology, immunology, surgery, veterinary medicine, bioinformatics, core facilities, other departments, individuals and labs. Qualifications Applicants should have a PhD, MD, MD/PhD, DVM, or equivalent doctoral degree in a relevant field, including biology, physiology, molecular biology, microbiology, immunology, pathology, biomedical sciences, nutrition, or related disciplines. Experience with cell culture, organoid systems, molecular biology, animal models, gastrointestinal biology, liver biology, microbiome research, immunology, histology, transcriptomics, metabolomics, or bioinformatics is desirable. Prior experience with large animal models is helpful. The ideal candidate will be highly motivated, organized, detail-oriented, and able to work both independently and collaboratively. Strong written and oral communication skills are important. Candidates with an interest in translational pediatric gastrointestinal and liver research, intestinal failure, epithelial biology, bile acid signaling, host-microbe interactions, inflammation, or organ crosstalk are especially encouraged to apply. Application Materials Interested applicants should submit a cover letter describing research interests and career goals, a curriculum vitae, and contact information for three references. Function Research Support Scheduled Weekly Hours: 40 Saint Louis University is an equal opportunity/affirmative action employer. All qualified candidates will receive consideration for the position applied for without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, disability, marital status, sexual orientation, military/veteran status, gender identity, or other non-merit factors. If accommodations are needed for completing the application and/or with the interviewing process, please contact Human Resources at 314-977-5847."
    },
    "https://slu.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/SLU-Saint-Louis-MO/Corporate-Relations-Specialist_2025-09293-1": {
      "title": "Corporate Relations Specialist",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-06\nFull time\n\nWho is Saint Louis University? Founded in 1818, Saint Louis University is one of the nation’s oldest and most prestigious Catholic universities. SLU, which also has a campus in Madrid, Spain, is recognized for world-class academics, life-changing research, compassionate health care, and a strong commitment to faith and service. JOB SUMMARY The Corporate Relations Specialist is responsible for increasing registrations and revenue for the Workforce Center. This position builds relationships with clients, partners, and associations to make the Center visible in the community. PRIMARY JOB RESPONSIBILITIES Initiates sales process by prospecting, scheduling appointments, understanding business needs, developing proposals and closing training opportunities to meet sales targets and metrics for increased revenue growth for the University’s Workforce Center set by the Executive Director Identifies, develops and implements account plans and awareness by introducing additional solutions and services provided by the University’s Workforce Center Attends events that help promote and market continuing education in the in the business professional community Opens and maintains lines of communication with clients and prospects Assists with daily operations in the University’s Workforce Center Performs other duties as assigned   KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS, AND ABILITIES Strong proficiency in use of software systems including a Customer Relationship Management (CRM) system like Salesforce Proven track record with selling services to corporations Strong written and verbal communication Strong interpersonal and presentation skills Ability to negotiate with corporations Ability to travel locally and work flexible hours MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS Bachelor’s degree Two years of related work experience PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS Previous experience in marketing, sales, or public relations Remote/In-Person Expectations This position will require the individual to work primarily in the office, with the flexibility to work up to one day per week remotely upon completion of the first 6 months of initial onsite training and familiarizing with department work and operations in compliance with the requirements of the SLU Remote Staff Flexible Work Policy. BENEFITS: Saint Louis University offers excellent full-time benefits including vacation and sick leave, health/dental/vision/life insurance, 403B retirement savings plan and match, tuition remission , employee assistance program, and wellness program. Function Student Support Scheduled Weekly Hours: 40 Saint Louis University is an equal opportunity/affirmative action employer. All qualified candidates will receive consideration for the position applied for without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, disability, marital status, sexual orientation, military/veteran status, gender identity, or other non-merit factors. If accommodations are needed for completing the application and/or with the interviewing process, please contact Human Resources at 314-977-5847."
    },
    "https://slu.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/SLU-Saint-Louis-MO/Executive-Director--Interdisciplinary-Center-for-Autism-Services_2026-09950": {
      "title": "Executive Director, Interdisciplinary Center for Autism Services",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-03\nFull time\n\nWho is Saint Louis University? Founded in 1818, Saint Louis University is one of the nation’s oldest and most prestigious Catholic universities. SLU, which also has a campus in Madrid, Spain, is recognized for world-class academics, life-changing research, compassionate health care, and a strong commitment to faith and service. ABOUT THE CENTER Established in 2019 within Saint Louis University’s School of Education , the Interdisciplinary Center for Autism Services (ICAS) provides diagnostic evaluation, parent education, social skills programming, and support navigating educational and community services for individuals with autism and their families. ICAS is entering a period of growth, with plans to expand interdisciplinary clinical services across the lifespan, community and school partnerships, and interdisciplinary training for students and professionals. JOB SUMMARY The Executive Director provides visionary, strategic, and operational leadership for the Interdisciplinary Center for Autism Services (ICAS). Reporting directly to the Dean of the School of Education, the Executive Director is responsible for building and sustaining a high-functioning, mission-driven center that serves individuals with autism and behavioral health needs while advancing Saint Louis University's commitment to research, education, and community engagement. The Executive Director will manage day-to-day operations, develop and steward external funding to support research and services, and represent ICAS and SLU with community partners, funders, and university stakeholders. This position is being funded by a grant and/or designated source, and therefore continuation in the position is contingent upon funding availability. PRIMARY JOB RESPONSIBILITIES Leadership & Strategy Provides leadership for ICAS, strengthening its operational infrastructure, staffing model, culture, policies, and procedures to support continued growth and increased capacity Develops and implements a strategic plan aligned with the Center's mission and the priorities of Saint Louis University and the School of Education Provide leadership and supervision for ICAS clinicians and staff and foster a collaborative, interdisciplinary team environment Operations & Administration Manages the day-to-day operations of the Center, including staffing, budgeting, facilities, and resource allocation systems for monitoring service delivery, program outcomes, financial performance, and organization effectiveness Fundraising & External Relations Develop and pursue external funding opportunities, including grants and philanthropic support, to advance the Center’s programs and long-term sustainability Build and maintain relationships with community organizations, school districts, funders, philanthropic partners, and state and federal agencies Represent ICAS with university and community stakeholders and in relevant public and professional settings Lead the expansion and implementation of interdisciplinary clinical services across the lifespan Ensure compliance with relevant regulatory, accreditation, billing, reimbursement, and ethical standards Establish Workforce & Academic Integration, & Research Partner with SLU faculty to integrate ICAS activities with graduate and undergraduate education and expand practicum, fieldwork, and clinical training opportunities across disciplines Partner with faculty and university research leaders to advance interdisciplinary applied research and program evaluation connected to the Center’s work Promote evidence-based practice, continuous learning, and dissemination of research and program outcomes KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS, AND ABILITIES Knowledge of autism, neurodevelopmental, and related services across the lifespan Knowledge of clinical program administration, including regulatory compliance, billing and reimbursement systems, and personnel management Knowledge of academic, clinical, and community partnership models that integrate research, education, and service Knowledge of grant funding, donor relations, and philanthropic partnership development Strong leadership and strategic planning skills, with the ability to translate vision into operational execution Strong verbal, written, and interpersonal communication skills, including the ability to represent ICAS to university leadership, funders, donors, and community partners Strong relationship-building skills across interdisciplinary and cross-institutional stakeholders Ability to lead interdisciplinary teams and clinical staff and foster a collaborative, mission-driven culture Ability to build and sustain partnerships that advance clinical, research, and educational goals Ability to use data to inform operational and strategic decision-making MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS Bachelor's degree Demonstrated experience in a leadership or program management role within a social services, clinical, or nonprofit setting PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS Master's or doctoral degree in education, social work, psychology, speech-language pathology, occupational therapy, business, nonprofit management, or a related field Demonstrated success in grant writing and securing external funding Knowledge of or experience working with neurodivergent populations, including individuals with autism, ADHD, or related developmental disabilities Demonstrated research background in autism, behavioral health, or related neurodevelopmental areas, including experience conducting, overseeing, or translating applied research into practice Experience working in or with an academic or university setting Applicants must include: 1) a cover letter; 2) a resume/curriculum vitae; You can upload these items on the third page \"My experience\" of the application. Initial application review will begin on October 20th and will continue on a rolling basis until the position is filled. Full-Time Benefits Saint Louis University offers a robust benefits package, such as tuition remission benefits for full-time employees and their dependents, comprehensive health coverage, generous retirement plans, and paid time off. Additionally, employees enjoy an inclusive community, wellness programs, and various discounts, all reflecting the university’s commitment to their well-being and success. Function Staff Program Support Scheduled Weekly Hours: 40 Saint Louis University is an equal opportunity/affirmative action employer. All qualified candidates will receive consideration for the position applied for without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, disability, marital status, sexual orientation, military/veteran status, gender identity, or other non-merit factors. If accommodations are needed for completing the application and/or with the interviewing process, please contact Human Resources at 314-977-5847."
    },
    "https://slu.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/SLU-Saint-Louis-MO/Nursing-Faculty-NTT---Public-Health_2026-09945": {
      "title": "Nursing Faculty NTT - Public Health",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-01\nFull time\n\nWho is Saint Louis University? Founded in 1818, Saint Louis University is one of the nation’s oldest and most prestigious Catholic universities. SLU, which also has a campus in Madrid, Spain, is recognized for world-class academics, life-changing research, compassionate health care, and a strong commitment to faith and service. Saint Louis University, a Catholic, Jesuit institution dedicated to student learning, research, health care and service, is seeking applicants for a non-tenure track faculty position in the School of Nursing. Saint Louis University is one of the premier Catholic universities in the United States, carrying on the 450 year old Jesuit tradition. The School of Nursing, an integral component of one of the largest Catholic health sciences centers in the world, has been in the forefront of nursing education since its founding in 1928. The School offers baccalaureate, master’s and doctoral (DNP and Ph.D.) programs and is accredited by the Commission on Collegiate Nursing Education. The School offers an infrastructure to support faculty research and practice and offers innovative curricula to effectively address current and future health care needs. Nominations and applications are invited for a non-tenure track appointment in the School of Nursing. This 9-month position requires: Graduate degree in nursing required; doctorate in nursing or a related field preferred Public Health, Medical Surgical nursing specialty Strong teaching and clinical skills with the ability to teach at undergraduate and/or graduate levels Licensure or eligibility for licensure in the state of Missouri Salary is dependent on qualifications and experience. Applicants must include: 1) a cover letter 2) a resume/curriculum vitae You can upload these items on the third page \"My experience\" of the application. All other correspondence regarding this position can be sent to: Saint Louis University School of Nursing, Search Committee Chair, 3525 Caroline Mall, St. Louis, MO 63104. kathleen.armstrong@slu.edu Review of applications will begin upon receipt and will continue until the position is filled . Function Nonmedical Primary Appointment <12 mo. Scheduled Weekly Hours: 40 Saint Louis University is an equal opportunity/affirmative action employer. All qualified candidates will receive consideration for the position applied for without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, disability, marital status, sexual orientation, military/veteran status, gender identity, or other non-merit factors. If accommodations are needed for completing the application and/or with the interviewing process, please contact Human Resources at 314-977-5847."
    },
    "https://slu.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/SLU-Saint-Louis-MO/IRB-Analyst-II_2026-10109": {
      "title": "IRB Analyst II",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-01\nFull time\n\nWho is Saint Louis University? Founded in 1818, Saint Louis University is one of the nation’s oldest and most prestigious Catholic universities. SLU, which also has a campus in Madrid, Spain, is recognized for world-class academics, life-changing research, compassionate health care, and a strong commitment to faith and service. JOB SUMMARY The IRB Analyst II coordinates the daily activities associated with the processing of research protocols and all facets of protocol review management to assist the Institutional Review Board (IRB) and Human Research Protection Program (HRPP); performs audits and monitoring visits under the IRB’s Quality Assurance Review (QAR) program; assists institutional research educational activities related to human subjects protections; assists with the training of HRPP staff. PRIMARY JOB RESPONSIBILITIES Reviews and processes exempt and expedited protocol submissions as an IRB designee; coordinates the review process of protocol submissions with IRB reviewers and, when deemed necessary, ancillary office reviewers; determines difficulty level of protocol issues and regulatory determinations; prepares protocols for IRB action; delineates revision requirements; reviews investigators’ responses; makes decisions for approval; aid reviewers’ and HRPP Director in approval decisions; processes or administratively withdraws protocols based on established guidelines Facilitates the review of all central IRBs, external IRBs, and single IRB submissions; reviews HRPP policies/procedures relative to central IRBs, external IRBs, and single IRB submissions to ensure that all SLU workflows and guidelines are followed and meet current federal regulations Coordinates IRB meetings; prepares agenda and materials to meet distribution deadlines; reviews materials with HRPP Director and Chairs; prepares draft meeting minutes; documents IRB review determinations; monitors existing and new protocols; gathers information and background material in response to inquiries/issues raised and to make approval decisions; responds to requests for information regarding IRB review Assists with all quality assurance efforts, including PI quality assurance reviews (QAR) and for-cause and noncompliance audits; monitors human subject research protocols for measures of overall compliance; assists with the analysis/summary of results, identification of alternatives for resolution of issues, and development and monitoring of corrective and preventative action plans (CAPA) Assists with revisions and implementation of HRPP forms, policies, guidelines, and standard operating procedures; assists with development of materials required for attaining and renewing accreditation by the Association for the Accreditation of Human Research Protection Programs (AAHRPP); assists in the development and presentation of training and seminars to faculty, staff, and students pertaining to research issues and institutional review requirements and processes Serves as liaison to assigned academic units; supports researchers through the IRB process; attends workshops and conferences focused on current issues affecting the IRB oversight of the protection of human subjects in research; informs Director of issues raised by the IRB or researchers Assists with the training of HRPP staff, which may include Analysts I, Coordinators, or other support positions; performs internal quality assurance reviews (iQARs) of the work completed by Analysts I and II and provides constructive feedback Performs other duties as assigned KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS, AND ABILITIES Extensive knowledge of ICH/GCP guidelines, FDA regulations, OHRP regulations, HIPAA Privacy Rule, and HRPP policies and guidelines related to human subject protection, medical and clinical terminology, and research methodology and design Strong analytical skills with ability to identify issues and solve problems within the framework of federal and state regulations, accreditation standards and institutional requirements Excellent verbal and written communication skills Professional demeanor with ability to work both collaboratively and independently, to maintain confidentiality, and to provide excellent customer service Ability to operate personal computers, Microsoft Office products, and customized data base software Good organizational skills with ability to work on multiple projects simultaneously Flexibility and ability to adapt to a changing environment MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS Bachelor’s degree Two or more years of current and relevant experience conducting, reviewing, and/or monitoring research involving human subjects Must hold CIP (Certified IRB Professional) certification PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS Master's degree Function Research Support Scheduled Weekly Hours: 40 Saint Louis University is an equal opportunity/affirmative action employer. All qualified candidates will receive consideration for the position applied for without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, disability, marital status, sexual orientation, military/veteran status, gender identity, or other non-merit factors. If accommodations are needed for completing the application and/or with the interviewing process, please contact Human Resources at 314-977-5847."
    },
    "https://slu.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/SLU-Saint-Louis-MO/Course-Reserves-and-Resource-Sharing-Specialist_2026-10099": {
      "title": "Course Reserves and Resource Sharing Specialist",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-29\nFull time\n\nWho is Saint Louis University? Founded in 1818, Saint Louis University is one of the nation’s oldest and most prestigious Catholic universities. SLU, which also has a campus in Madrid, Spain, is recognized for world-class academics, life-changing research, compassionate health care, and a strong commitment to faith and service. JOB SUMMARY   The Course Reserves and Resource Sharing Specialist administers print and electronic course reserve services, ensuring that instructional materials are accessible to students and providing timely support to instructors. This position supports inter-library loan and resource-sharing requests, provides frontline service at the circulation desk and assists with department operations, student employee training and library access services. Working hours are from Monday through Friday, 10:00am - 6:00pm. During breaks and summer, the shift hours may change to meet the library’s operating hours. PRIMARY JOB RESPONSIBILITIES   Course Reserves Oversees all aspects of print and electronic course reserve services, including adding/removing materials and creating electronic records to build the Reserve Collection database. Serves as primary contact for instructors regarding Course Reserve materials. Assists and advises faculty and staff on the use of the Reserve Collection, assuring that items placed on reserve comply with Copyright Fair Use, or obtain permission through the Copyright Clearance Center or by direct contact with individual publishers. Pays invoices from the Copyright Clearance Center and inform the Administration of payments. Compiles and maintains the Course Reserves Procedures Manual to standardize policy. Provides training on reserve procedures. Trains and provides direction to student assistants supporting reserves. Gathers and provides statistical data regarding reserves. Service, Communication & Problem Solving Performs circulation duties within Access & Delivery Services department. Provides frontline customer service at the circulation desk by assisting patrons with borrowing, returning, and renewing library materials Manages patron accounts, billing issues, overdue materials, and access-related concerns. Opens and closes the library as assigned and help maintain the security of the building and collections. Responds to user questions, assists with basic reference and directional questions, and guides users in navigating databases, conducting searches, and locating materials. Processes library holds. Maintains a good understanding of library policies to address any patron inquiries. Assists with training, supervision, and evaluation of student assistants. Collects and monitors statistics needed for operational efficiency. Inter-library Loan Support Under the direction of Interlibrary Loan Coordinator, assists with the processing of interlibrary loan requests. Processes incoming and outcoming interlibrary loan requests in accordance with establishing library procedures and resource-sharing guidelines. Retrieves, scans, copies, and prepares library materials for delivery to requesting patrons or lending libraries. Receives and processes materials borrowed from other libraries and ensure timely notification and delivery to patrons. Communicates with patrons and participating libraries regarding the status of requests. Processes renewals, returns, cancellations and other routine updates associated with interlibrary loan transactions. Collaboration & Professional Development Supports the library’s mission, vision, and values. Contributes to the advancement of the library’s strategic plan. Prepares, reviews, maintains, and assists with a variety of related reports, records, and documents. Cooperates as a team member with library staff in performing any duties essential to efficient library services. Participates in committees and groups in support of library’s strategic plan implementation. Participates in ongoing professional development and stay current regarding library related practices, technology, and equipment. KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS, AND ABILITIES   Knowledge of academic library access, circulation, course reserve and resource-sharing practices  Knowledge of copyright and fair use principles applicable to course reserve services  Knowledge of integrated library systems, database applications and content management systems  Knowledge of best practices in academic research libraries and Access and Delivery Services  Strong customer service, communication and interpersonal skills  Ability to interpret and address user needs  Ability to de-escalate difficult or complex situations  Ability to explain technical information and processes clearly  Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with the University community  Ability to manage multiple priorities and meet deadlines  Ability to train and provide direction to student assistants  Ability to contribute to the library mission, strategic goals and commitment to serving a diverse university community MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS   Bachelor's degree  Two years of library experience obtained within the previous five years or an equivalent combination of current library experience, training, and/or education in related fields Proficiency with library-specific applications, including integrated library systems, database applications and content management systems PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS   Experience supervising student employees  Experience in an academic research library or Access and Delivery Services environment  Applicants must include: 1) a cover letter 2) a resume/curriculum vitae You can upload these items on the third page \"My experience\" of the application. Function Libraries Scheduled Weekly Hours: 40 Saint Louis University is an equal opportunity/affirmative action employer. All qualified candidates will receive consideration for the position applied for without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, disability, marital status, sexual orientation, military/veteran status, gender identity, or other non-merit factors. If accommodations are needed for completing the application and/or with the interviewing process, please contact Human Resources at 314-977-5847."
    },
    "https://slu.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/SLU-Saint-Louis-MO/Occupational-Health-Program-Manager_2026-10102": {
      "title": "Occupational Health Program Manager",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-24\nFull time\n\nWho is Saint Louis University? Founded in 1818, Saint Louis University is one of the nation’s oldest and most prestigious Catholic universities. SLU, which also has a campus in Madrid, Spain, is recognized for world-class academics, life-changing research, compassionate health care, and a strong commitment to faith and service. JOB SUMMARY The Occupational Health Program Manager manages the provision of an efficient, high quality Occupational Health Program for Laboratory and Animal Research (OHP) service for University staff. This position ensures compliance with the responsibilities imposed by health and safety accrediting organizations. This position is also responsible for reducing the risk of cases of occupational injury/illness, and championing best practices in occupational health provision within the University. PRIMARY JOB RESPONSIBILITIES Plans, develops, coordinates, monitors, and audits the delivery of OHP services provided to the University; ensures high quality, customer satisfaction; promotes best practice in OHP based on research, evidence, and evaluation  Formulates, implements, and evaluates policies/strategies for health protection and surveillance of workers to meet regulatory requirements and to promote OHP participants’ health and wellbeing Works in partnership with Research leadership and other appropriate professionals/agencies to provide expert guidance when OHP input is required; maintains good relationships to develop the understanding and involvement of the OHP in the support of laboratory and animal research workers Develops processes for gathering data for continued improvement; communicates trends and advises on action plans to meet regulatory requirements Responsible for the maintenance of a confidential records management system Contributes to the provision of training, advice, health surveillance, vaccinations, respirator physicals/fit tests, sickness absence management, investigations of cases of occupational injury/illness, and other general OHP issues Stays abreast of new and emerging guidance and regulations that govern OHP practice; resources for this include ACOEM (American College of Occupational and Environmental Medicine), as well as the Eagleson Institute; uses evidence-based practice to guide interpretation of statutory requirements and advisory guidance to ensure the health protection of OHP participants Assists in creating new services for OHP participants Performs other duties as assigned KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS, AND ABILITIES Familiarity with OSHA regulations, to include 29 CFR 1910, 29 CFR 1926, 29 CFR 1904, and 29 CFR 1960 Strong written and verbal communication skills Strong skills with Microsoft Office software and utilization of information systems MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS Registered Nurse (RN) or Advanced Nurse Practitioner (ANP) Four or more years of experience in occupational safety and health PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS Previous experience in safety, industrial hygiene, environmental health, health physics, biology, or other safety related field Previous experience in federal government Function Research Support Scheduled Weekly Hours: 40 Saint Louis University is an equal opportunity/affirmative action employer. All qualified candidates will receive consideration for the position applied for without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, disability, marital status, sexual orientation, military/veteran status, gender identity, or other non-merit factors. If accommodations are needed for completing the application and/or with the interviewing process, please contact Human Resources at 314-977-5847."
    },
    "https://slu.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/SLU-Saint-Louis-MO/Senior-Geospatial-Research-Scientist_2026-10091": {
      "title": "Geospatial Research Scientist",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-24\nFull time\n\nWho is Saint Louis University? Founded in 1818, Saint Louis University is one of the nation’s oldest and most prestigious Catholic universities. SLU, which also has a campus in Madrid, Spain, is recognized for world-class academics, life-changing research, compassionate health care, and a strong commitment to faith and service. JOB SUMMARY The Geospatial Research Scientist or Senior Geospatial Research Scientist leads innovative research initiatives in geospatial science, remote sensing, and GeoAI, applying advanced analytics, machine learning, and image processing techniques to address complex challenges in areas such as greenhouse gas emissions, environmental monitoring, and precision agriculture. This position is responsible for developing research concepts, designing and executing experiments, analyzing and integrating multi-source geospatial data, and disseminating findings through publications, presentations, and sponsored research proposals. The Geospatial Research Scientist or Senior Geospatial Research Scientist collaborates with interdisciplinary teams, contributes to strategic partnerships and funding development, and supports the advancement of cutting-edge research within Saint Louis University's Remote Sensing Lab.   PRIMARY JOB RESPONSIBILITIES Identify compelling scientific questions, design experiments, and conduct ground-breaking research Participate in securing external funding by developing grant proposals Liaison to coordinate projects and support interdisciplinary collaboration Drafting peer-reviewed publications and project reports Process and analyze drone and satellite data (e.g., WorldView, Planet, SAR) Participate in field surveys, deploying calibration sites Performs other duties as assigned   KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS, AND ABILITIES Strong foundational knowledge in remote sensing, image processing, and geospatial data collection and analysis Synthetic Aperture Radar (SAR)  Verbal and written communication skills, including presentations Strong interpersonal skills, including teamwork and collaboration Supervisory skills Ability to integrate interdisciplinary research concepts Demonstrated ability to collaborate, lead projects, and oversee and guide team members Proven ability to identify and pursue funding opportunities, developing proposals to secure grants from both academic and industry sources Expertise in integrating interdisciplinary research concepts to create innovative research applications Adaptability to work in a dynamic, fast-paced environment, identifying areas for improvement and collaborating with team members to address gaps   MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS FOR GEOSPATIAL RESEARCH SCIENTIST Master’s degree in geospatial science, geography, earth science, or closely related fields such as computer engineering, electronic engineering, computer science, or technology  Three years of related work experience   PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS FOR GEOSPATIAL RESEARCH SCIENTIST Ph.D. in geospatial science, geography or environmental science with geospatial concentration, computer engineering, electronic engineering, geospatial science, earth science or computer science and technology Strong programming, signal processing, cloud computing, and data analytical skills MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS FOR SENIOR GEOSPATIAL RESEARCH SCIENTIST Master’s degree in geospatial science, geography, earth science, or closely related fields such as computer engineering, electronic engineering, computer science, or technology  Five years of related work experience Project management experience and external engagement Demonstrated experience in building collaborations, leading projects, and overseeing, and guiding team members   PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS FOR SENIOR GEOSPATIAL RESEARCH SCIENTIST PhD in geospatial science, geoinformatics, geography, computer science, remote sensing, or related areas with strong geospatial skills Record of scholarly research and publications Appointment level will be commensurate with the selected candidate's qualifications and experience. Candidates meeting the qualifications for Senior Geospatial Research Scientist may be appointed at the senior level based on demonstrated research leadership, project management experience, scholarly achievements, and ability to support the growth and strategic objectives of the Remote Sensing Lab. ABOUT THE REMOTE SENSING LAB (RSL) The Remote Sensing Lab advances geospatial science through machine learning and AI-driven analysis of multi-scale remote sensing data to tackle pressing challenges in food and water security, environmental change, and socio-ecological resilience. Its research combines geospatial computer vision, digital twins and photogrammetry, and sensor fusion—integrating satellite, UAV, and field-based hyperspectral, multispectral, thermal, and LiDAR measurements to monitor agriculture, ecosystems, and land-use dynamics. Active projects span quantum farming and precision agriculture, remote sensing based nitrogen prescriptions to boost crop productivity, early detection of plant diseases, identification of biological and chemical stressors, carbon accounting, permafrost material chemistry, and development of a global InSAR accuracy model. Supported by high-performance computing and advanced imaging systems, the lab delivers innovative GeoAI solutions that drive sustainable agriculture, strengthen food security, and deepen understanding of land-water-climate interactions. Function Research Support Scheduled Weekly Hours: 40 Saint Louis University is an equal opportunity/affirmative action employer. All qualified candidates will receive consideration for the position applied for without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, disability, marital status, sexual orientation, military/veteran status, gender identity, or other non-merit factors. If accommodations are needed for completing the application and/or with the interviewing process, please contact Human Resources at 314-977-5847."
    },
