    "https://slu.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/Texas-State_Remote-Residence/Regional-Admission-Program-Coordinator---Texas_2026-10067": {
      "title": "Regional Admission Program Coordinator - Texas",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-18\nFull time\n\nWho is Saint Louis University? Founded in 1818, Saint Louis University is one of the nation’s oldest and most prestigious Catholic universities. SLU, which also has a campus in Madrid, Spain, is recognized for world-class academics, life-changing research, compassionate health care, and a strong commitment to faith and service. JOB SUMMARY The Regional Admission Program Coordinator supports the institution’s enrollment goals by engaging with prospective students and families throughout the admission process. This position manages a regional recruitment territory and home office and assists in the overall operation of the office of admission. This position demonstrates understanding and sensitivity to the needs of all students, and performs duties in accordance with the values of a Jesuit, liberal arts education. Additionally, the Regional Admission Program Coordinator serves as a liaison to faculty, academic departments, and other University stakeholders to effectively communicate enrollment information and collaborates regarding recruitment activities and pre-professional opportunities.     PRIMARY JOB RESPONSIBILITIES Manages a regional recruitment territory and home office; develops recruitment strategies; travels the designated recruitment territory up to 30%; maintains an informational, active communication system with either traditional high school, parents or counselors; assumes liaison activities for the Office of Admission Counsels student applicants concerning admission, financial aid, career planning, and housing options; explains, interprets, and provides outreach to students regarding the FAFSA and financial aid awards Identifies, recruits, and enrolls prospective students in a designated market; manages a recruitment territory; develops recruitment strategies Plans and arranges all phases of travel; conducts office-based contact by text, email and phone with students, and parents if applicable; may make reservations; assists with administrative duties in support of student recruitment Reads, interprets, and evaluates students’ academic credentials and makes admission/denial decisions; assists with scholarship appropriation Participates positively as an active member of the recruitment team; assists with special programs and research projects; participates in the development and implementation of enrollment strategies Perform various administrative tasks, to include composing routine letters, compiling data for reports, maintaining calendars, processing applications, scheduling appointments, maintains confidential files, prepares position papers/reports, inputs/retrieves data on information system software, etc. Performs other duties as assigned     KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS, AND ABILITIES Knowledge of higher education admission policies and programs Knowledge of enrollment planning strategies Interpersonal/human relations skills Verbal and written communication skills Effective presentation skills Planning and organizational skills Basic research skills Ability to demonstrate self-direction and motivation Ability to operate personal computer with various software programs Ability to maintain confidentiality Ability to learn and apply institutional policies and procedures Ability to maintain schedules Ability to work effectively in a team setting Ability to travel/drive and work on weekends and nights Ability to handle stress due to travel  Ability to multi-task and deal with competing priorities Ability to build relationships with and recruit a diverse population of students in all parts of the United States   MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS Bachelor's Degree Two years of related work experience Previous experience working with a CRM  Applicants must have a valid driver's license and maintain active personal car insurance with sufficient limits throughout the duration of employment. Ability to rent a car, fly, ability to book a hotel for overnight travel, and ability to travel locally. The scope of the position requires working some evenings, weekends, and out-of-town travel, including overnight stays. This is a regional position based in Texas.   PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS Previous experience working with Slate Applicants must include: 1) a cover letter; 2) a resume/curriculum vitae.  You can upload these items on the third page \"My experience\" of the application Full-Time Benefits: Saint Louis University offers a generous full-time benefits package including vacation and sick leave, health/dental/vision/life insurance, 403B retirement savings plan and match, tuition remission benefits , employee assistance program and wellness program. Function Student Support Scheduled Weekly Hours: 40 Saint Louis University is an equal opportunity/affirmative action employer. All qualified candidates will receive consideration for the position applied for without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, disability, marital status, sexual orientation, military/veteran status, gender identity, or other non-merit factors. If accommodations are needed for completing the application and/or with the interviewing process, please contact Human Resources at 314-977-5847."
    },
    "https://slu.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/SLU-Saint-Louis-MO/Maintenance-A-Worker---General_2026-09669": {
      "title": "Maintenance A Worker - General",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-17\nFull time\n\nWho is Saint Louis University? Founded in 1818, Saint Louis University is one of the nation’s oldest and most prestigious Catholic universities. SLU, which also has a campus in Madrid, Spain, is recognized for world-class academics, life-changing research, compassionate health care, and a strong commitment to faith and service. Position Summary Perform routine and preventative maintenance at the University campus with a strong focus on HVAC systems. Address service requests from faculty, staff, and students, and complete assigned work orders from facilities supervisors. Responsibilities include inspections, troubleshooting, repairs, and minor installations related to heating, cooling, and ventilation systems, ensuring reliable and safe operation across multiple campus buildings. Primary Duties and Responsibilities: Service Calls & Emergency Response Provide responsive, customer-focused service. Deliver courteous, timely support for faculty, staff, and student concerns. Prioritize and complete work orders efficiently. Assess issues and determine when escalation or specialized support is needed. Support special events and room setups. Routine Maintenance & Repairs Perform basic repairs to walls, floors, ceilings, windows, and doors. Execute patching, painting, caulking, and general upkeep. Replace light bulbs, ceiling tiles, hardware, and furniture components. Building Systems Support Must be able to perform light troubleshooting of HVAC, plumbing, and electrical as needed. Report issues requiring skilled trades or contractors. Preventative Maintenance Perform scheduled building inspections and maintenance tasks. Ensure cleanliness, safety, and readiness of building common areas. Check and maintain equipment such as sump pumps, filters, and fans. Documentation & Reporting Maintain accurate records of work performed and equipment serviced Report on building issues or safety concerns to supervisors Working Conditions: Require standing, bending, climbing, lifting up to 50 pounds, and working on ladders or at heights. Work may occur indoors and outdoors, in varying weather and temperature conditions. Exposure to pool chemicals, noise, and mechanical equipment is expected. May be required to work flexible hours including evenings, weekends, or on-call shifts for emergencies. Required Qualifications High school diploma or equivalent. Valid Class E driver’s license (or equivalent from another state). Must be available 24/7 for emergencies and willing to work overtime. Preferred Qualifications Two-year degree or certification in a technical field. Five or more years of experience in facilities maintenance Position requires background check and other applicable pre-employment checks. Benefits for this position are in accordance with the collective bargaining agreement with IUOE Local 148. Union employees receive health, retirement, and tuition benefits, as well as sick time and paid vacation. Hourly wage is $33.86 per hour. Function Maintenance Worker Scheduled Weekly Hours: 40 Saint Louis University is an equal opportunity/affirmative action employer. All qualified candidates will receive consideration for the position applied for without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, disability, marital status, sexual orientation, military/veteran status, gender identity, or other non-merit factors. If accommodations are needed for completing the application and/or with the interviewing process, please contact Human Resources at 314-977-5847."
    },
    "https://slu.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/SLU-Saint-Louis-MO/Program-Coordinator-III---SOM-Year-2_2026-10059-1": {
      "title": "Program Coordinator III - SOM Year 2",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-16\nFull time\n\nWho is Saint Louis University? Founded in 1818, Saint Louis University is one of the nation’s oldest and most prestigious Catholic universities. SLU, which also has a campus in Madrid, Spain, is recognized for world-class academics, life-changing research, compassionate health care, and a strong commitment to faith and service. JOB SUMMARY The Program Coordinator III (Year 2) provides administrative and operational support for Year 2 medical school courses and related academic programs. This position coordinates academic operations, supports faculty and students, manages course materials and evaluations, maintains curricular systems, and provides administrative support for committees and governance processes. The position serves as a key liaison among faculty, students, academic leadership, and institutional systems to ensure efficient and compliant program operations. PRIMARY JOB RESPONSIBILITIES Provides centralized administrative oversight for all Year 2 courses and ensures syllabi, schedules, examinations, and instructional materials are accurate, timely, and compliant with institutional and accreditation requirements Serves as the primary operational liaison between course directors, faculty, students, and curricular systems including OASIS and ExamSoft Coordinates room scheduling, examination preparation and proctoring, post-examination processing, academic calendar maintenance, and curricular website updates Manages course and faculty evaluations and prepares and distributes evaluation reports to faculty and department leadership Provides administrative support for the Preclinical Subcommittee, Program Evaluation and Assessment Subcommittee, and other committees as assigned Schedules evaluation meetings, secures meeting space, coordinates catering, and assists with meeting setup and cleanup activities Provides complex administrative support by coordinating meetings and appointments, researching and compiling information, preparing reports and correspondence, and arranging travel accommodations Assists in planning and implementing programs, projects, activities, and services and may independently coordinate assigned initiatives Compiles and develops budgets; monitors expenditures; processes invoices, payroll, and account reconciliations; and prepares financial reports as assigned Attends meetings and provides administrative and clerical support to committees, commissions, and task forces as required Establishes and maintains recordkeeping systems and supports implementation of information technology systems within assigned areas Provides front-office support for students, faculty, staff, and visitors and assists faculty with instructional technologies including Panopto and audience response systems Handles confidential information and sensitive records using discretion and sound judgment May supervise, train, and delegate work to clerical staff and coordinate employee training activities Performs general office functions including ordering supplies, maintaining records, and performing basic bookkeeping activities Performs other duties as assigned KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS, AND ABILITIES Knowledge of administrative and clerical procedures, office systems, records management, and business practices Knowledge of customer service principles and processes, including customer needs assessment and service quality standards Knowledge of interpersonal techniques utilizing tact, patience, and professionalism Strong verbal and written communication skills Knowledge of English grammar, spelling, punctuation, and business correspondence standards Proficiency with computers, assigned software applications, and office technologies Ability to provide support and technical assistance to internal and external stakeholders Ability to maintain accurate and confidential records and files Ability to meet deadlines and manage multiple priorities Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with diverse groups Ability to work independently with minimal supervision Ability to conduct research and compile reports Ability to maintain confidentiality of sensitive and privileged information Ability to analyze situations and implement effective solutions Ability to maintain consistent, punctual, and reliable attendance MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS High school diploma Five years of relevant administrative, program coordination, or office support experience Function Staff Program Support Scheduled Weekly Hours: 40 Saint Louis University is an equal opportunity/affirmative action employer. All qualified candidates will receive consideration for the position applied for without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, disability, marital status, sexual orientation, military/veteran status, gender identity, or other non-merit factors. If accommodations are needed for completing the application and/or with the interviewing process, please contact Human Resources at 314-977-5847."
    },
    "https://slu.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/SLU-Saint-Louis-MO/Marketing-Manager--School-of-Medicine_2026-10085": {
      "title": "Marketing Manager, School of Medicine",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-09\nFull time\n\nWho is Saint Louis University? Founded in 1818, Saint Louis University is one of the nation’s oldest and most prestigious Catholic universities. SLU, which also has a campus in Madrid, Spain, is recognized for world-class academics, life-changing research, compassionate health care, and a strong commitment to faith and service. Position Summary The Marketing Manager for SLU School of Medicine serves as the lead Marketing and Communications partner for the School of Medicine. Acting as a trusted advisor, this role is responsible for translating School of Medicine mission and goals, including medical (MD) and graduate program education, community outreach, research, and other priorities of the School of Medicine, into strategic, multi-channel marketing and communications plans that align with University priorities and brand standards. The Marketing Manager coordinates with Marketing and Communications (MarCom) colleagues to deliver campaigns on time, on budget, and on goal, fostering collaboration and measurable impact across the University . The ideal candidate brings both a strategic mindset and hands-on execution skills : a strong marketing background, excellent listening and relationship-building abilities, and a track record of turning complex needs into clear, actionable plans and well-executed initiatives. They inspire trust, balance multiple priorities with ease, and thrive in a collaborative, mission-driven environment rooted in Jesuit values. Key Responsibilities Marketing Planning and Implementation Help lead the development of integrated, multi-channel marketing and communications strategies that drive enrollment, reputation, revenue, and student success. Collaborate with School of Medicine partners and MarCom experts to align marketing efforts and strategic communications, including social media, web content, print, and internal and external messaging. Translate strategies into actionable marketing initiatives; develop creative briefs and project roadmaps; manage task lists and timelines to guide content, design, and channel strategy. Execute marketing campaigns across paid media, web, and social channels, engaging cross-functional teams of subject matter experts, writers, designers, and vendor partners as needed, to deliver campaigns from conception through execution and evaluation. Monitor plan execution, timelines, and budgets, proactively addressing risks or barriers to success to ensure follow through. Oversee performance tracking, working closely with vendor partners when applicable. Use performance metrics and analytics to inform data-driven recommendations and continuous improvement. Uphold SLU’s brand strategy, visual identity, and editorial standards across all projects. Campus Partner Engagement Serve as the primary liaison for the School of Medicine, working with unit experts to regularly assess needs, gather insights, and identify priorities and objectives. Facilitate collaboration between campus partners and MarCom colleagues, ensuring transparency, alignment, and shared success. Identify and act on timely opportunities to advance University and campus-unit objectives. Interact with faculty, staff, and students to cultivate story ideas aligned with audience insights and strategic areas of expertise. Monitor relevant regional and national trends; develop a deep understanding of the health sciences sector and audiences; identify and develop newsworthy content and support the MarCom PR team on media placement opportunities and timely stories for amplification through owned channels. Collaborate closely with unit and admission partners throughout the prospective student journey to optimize marketing and communication channels at each phase. Provide strategic counsel to campus partners and University leadership, grounded in higher education marketing trends and data insights. Minimum Qualifications Bachelor’s degree in Marketing, Communications, Business, or related field. 5+ years of progressive experience in marketing, paid media strategy, and/or project management, ideally in an agency or in health care, medical education, higher education, or other complex organizations. Proven success leading integrated marketing and communications initiatives and cultivating strong relationships. Expertise in paid media tactics, platforms, tracking, automation, and emerging marketing technologies. Knowledge of channel strategy and content best practices across earned, owned and shared marketing channels. Exceptional interpersonal, organizational, and written/verbal communication skills. Ability to manage multiple priorities under tight deadlines while maintaining quality and attention to detail. Preferred Qualifications Marketing or advertising agency experience. Experience in higher education marketing, health sciences, or health care marketing. Familiarity with CRM platforms, project management tools (e.g., Asana, Monday, Trello, Wrike), and analytics dashboards. Knowledge of enrollment marketing, reputation-building, and stakeholder engagement. Why Join Us? At SLU, you’ll be part of a mission-driven university that’s shaping lives and communities around the globe. You’ll join a creative, collaborative team where your ideas matter, your expertise drives impact, and your work helps elevate one of the nation’s most distinctive Jesuit institutions. About Saint Louis University Founded in 1818, Saint Louis University is one of the nation’s oldest and most prestigious Catholic universities. SLU, which also has a campus in Madrid, Spain, is recognized for world-class academics, life-changing research, compassionate health care, and a strong commitment to faith and service. About the Division of Marketing and Communications The Division of Marketing and Communications serves as Saint Louis University’s core marketing, communications, brand, and digital strategy function. Our award-winning team of strategic and creative professionals advances the University’s mission by driving student recruitment and retention, supporting revenue generation and community engagement, amplifying research excellence, and building and protecting institutional reputation locally, nationally, and globally. We support institutional priorities through integrated strategies that include marketing, media relations, internal communications, digital content, and creative services. About the School of Medicine Saint Louis University School of Medicine , established in 1836, has a long tradition of excellence in teaching, research, and patient care. In addition to educating medical students, graduate students, and residents, the school is a leading center of research in infectious disease, liver disease, aging and brain disorders, immunology, and neuroscience. SLU’s medical school is located in St. Louis, Missouri, adjacent to SLU’s nursing and allied health schools and near SSM Health Saint Louis University Hospital and SSM Health Cardinal Glennon Hospital. Function Brand Management Scheduled Weekly Hours: 40 Saint Louis University is an equal opportunity/affirmative action employer. All qualified candidates will receive consideration for the position applied for without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, disability, marital status, sexual orientation, military/veteran status, gender identity, or other non-merit factors. If accommodations are needed for completing the application and/or with the interviewing process, please contact Human Resources at 314-977-5847."
    },
    "https://slu.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/Scott-Hall/Assistant-Associate-Professor-of-Law_2026-10043": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate/Professor of Law",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-09\nFull time\n\nWho is Saint Louis University? Founded in 1818, Saint Louis University is one of the nation’s oldest and most prestigious Catholic universities. SLU, which also has a campus in Madrid, Spain, is recognized for world-class academics, life-changing research, compassionate health care, and a strong commitment to faith and service. SAINT LOUIS UNIVERSITY SCHOOL OF LAW, a Catholic, Jesuit institution dedicated to student learning, research, health care, and social justice, seeks applicants for a tenure-track or tenured appointment in the School of Law, beginning Fall 2027. The School of Law seeks faculty members committed to excellence in teaching, engaged scholarship, and public service, with a principal focus on business, commercial, and contracts law. Candidates who can also teach real property are strongly preferred, as business law, commercial law, contracts, and real property are core curricular needs. Candidates with the ability to teach in international/comparative law or labor and employment law are a plus, particularly when paired with the core subjects above. Additional expertise in complementary specialties is welcome but secondary to the core teaching needs. Saint Louis University is an R1-designated Jesuit institution in the city of St. Louis. The School of Law is located downtown, just steps away from federal, state, and municipal courthouses. St. Louis boasts an affordable cost of living, easy commutes, and a strong housing market. Qualifications for this position include a J.D. degree, academic excellence, and outstanding teaching and scholarly promise. Consideration of applications and nominations for this position will begin as they are received and will continue until the position is filled. Applications should include a cover letter, CV, names of references, and information regarding teaching and scholarly interest(s), and may be submitted online. Please direct any questions to Professor Sam Jordan, Search Committee Chair, at slulawhiring@slu.edu. Function Nonmedical Primary Appointment <12 mo. Scheduled Weekly Hours: 40 Saint Louis University is an equal opportunity/affirmative action employer. All qualified candidates will receive consideration for the position applied for without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, disability, marital status, sexual orientation, military/veteran status, gender identity, or other non-merit factors. If accommodations are needed for completing the application and/or with the interviewing process, please contact Human Resources at 314-977-5847."
    },
    "https://slu.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/Macelwane-Hall/Postdoctoral-Research-Associate--Microbial-Ecology-Lab_2026-10081": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Research Associate, Microbial Ecology Lab",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-08\nFull time\n\nWho is Saint Louis University? Founded in 1818, Saint Louis University is one of the nation’s oldest and most prestigious Catholic universities. SLU, which also has a campus in Madrid, Spain, is recognized for world-class academics, life-changing research, compassionate health care, and a strong commitment to faith and service. The Soil Microbial Ecology Laboratory at Saint Louis University is looking for a creative post-doctoral scientist with strong background in soil microbiome, multi-omics [metagenomics/transcriptomics/metabolomics], as well as bioinformatics. Responsibilities: This researcher will assist the research team in conducting soil sampling in the field and assess soil functions using multi-omics analyses. The major tasks will include but are not limited: Quantify microbial functional genes using qPCR. Develop AI-driven bioinformatics pipeline and analyze multi-omics data. Perform soil sampling and experiment design. Measure soil properties—soil pH, moisture content, Inorganic N, etc. Soil incubation and activity measurement. Training undergrad and graduate students in the laboratory. Qualifications: Applicants should have the following qualifications to be considered: PhD in microbial ecology/microbiology, and bioinformatics or related field. Experience in multi-omics pipeline development and analyses are required. Experience in wet lab: soil incubation, qPCR, DNA/RNA extraction. Evidence of scientific productivity in the form of peer-reviewed publications. Ability to take a leadership role for the project. Salary and Benefits: Salary is commensurate with experience. Health insurance benefits are provided. The appointment is for 1 year with the possibility of an additional year pending satisfactory progress. Application Deadline: This position will be open until it is filled. Application: Interested applicants should send (1) a cover letter detailing the applicant’s research experience and starting date availability, (2) curriculum vitae, and (3) name, telephone numbers and e-mail addresses of three professional references to Dr. Laibin Huang ( laibin.huang@slu.edu ). Please, include the following in the subject line of the e-mail: “Your Last Name - Postdoc Application.” Equal opportunity/affirmative action Statement: Saint Louis University is an equal opportunity/affirmative action employer. All qualified candidates will receive consideration for the position applied for without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, disability, marital status, sexual orientation, military/veteran status, gender identity, or other non-merit factors. We welcome and encourage applications from minorities, women, protected veterans, and individuals with disabilities (including disabled veterans). If accommodation is needed for completing the application and/or with the interviewing process, please contact Human Resources at 314-977-5847. Critical or essential: The postdoc hire is critical to the department’s research mission and important for supporting ongoing research in Dr Huang’s Microbial Ecology Lab. The primary focus of this role is to support ongoing research, establish lab protocols, and generate preliminary data for securing extramural funding. Below are the specific aspects related to this position: a) Developing standard protocols for Molecular techniques. This will require different kinds of training skills, including field soil sampling and soil nutrients analyses, experimental design, gene clone, PCR and qPCR, sequence library preparation. These skills are critical for maintaining lab productivity and data integrity. b) Data analyses: skills in bioinformatics and high-throughput data analyses (metagenomic/transcriptomic analysis). These are critical for interpreting complex datasets and translating them into publications for supporting grant proposals. c) Mentoring and training graduate students: training the graduate students with these hands-on experiences and data analysis skills. This will strengthen the lab’s research output as well as the department’s mission of fostering high-quality training in graduate research. Function Research Support Scheduled Weekly Hours: 40 Saint Louis University is an equal opportunity/affirmative action employer. All qualified candidates will receive consideration for the position applied for without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, disability, marital status, sexual orientation, military/veteran status, gender identity, or other non-merit factors. If accommodations are needed for completing the application and/or with the interviewing process, please contact Human Resources at 314-977-5847."
    },
    "https://slu.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/McDonnell-Douglas-Hall/Post-Doctoral-Fellow---Yilmaz-lab_2026-10026": {
      "title": "Post Doctoral Fellow - Yilmaz lab",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-08-26\nFull time\n\nWho is Saint Louis University? Founded in 1818, Saint Louis University is one of the nation’s oldest and most prestigious Catholic universities. SLU, which also has a campus in Madrid, Spain, is recognized for world-class academics, life-changing research, compassionate health care, and a strong commitment to faith and service. Postdoctoral Scholar (Complex Photonics and Wave Control) Opportunity for a postdoctoral scholar is available in Dr. Hasan Yılmaz’s research group in the Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering at Saint Louis University for researchers with strong backgrounds in complex photonics, wave physics, mesoscopic physics, or related fields. The successful candidate will primarily carry out experimental research on complex photonics, wave control, and light transport in systems such as multiple-scattering media and multimode fibers. The position involves developing advanced optical experiments, conducting numerical simulations, and engaging closely with theoretical aspects of wave physics. Current research directions include wavefront shaping, transmission eigenchannels, mesoscopic correlations, spatiotemporal wave control, and the fundamental limits of light manipulation in complex systems. The candidate is expected to work closely with theoretical and experimental collaborators and supervise and mentor graduate students. Requirements: Ph.D. degree in Physics, Electrical Engineering, Applied Physics, Optical Sciences, or a related field. Proven track record in one or more of the fields mentioned above. Strong experimental background in optics or wave physics. Strong interest in theoretical aspects of wave propagation and complex systems. Experience with optical experiments, numerical simulations, or computational modeling. Programming and simulation skills in MATLAB, Python, COMSOL, Lumerical, or similar platforms are highly desirable. Excellent interpersonal communication and teamwork skills. Ability to work independently and collaboratively as part of a research team. Preferred Qualifications: Experience in one or more of the following areas is highly desirable: Wavefront shaping and spatial light modulator systems Multimode fiber optics Mesoscopic physics and statistical optics Interferometric measurements Optical system design and instrumentation Term/Availability: This is a limited-term appointment funded for one year from the date of hire with a strong possibility of renewal based on performance and funding availability. Job Classification: Postdoctoral Researcher Job Type: Full-time Applicants should submit a CV, a brief statement of research interests, and contact information for two references, preferably including the Ph.D. advisor. Function Research Support Scheduled Weekly Hours: 40 Saint Louis University is an equal opportunity/affirmative action employer. All qualified candidates will receive consideration for the position applied for without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, disability, marital status, sexual orientation, military/veteran status, gender identity, or other non-merit factors. If accommodations are needed for completing the application and/or with the interviewing process, please contact Human Resources at 314-977-5847."
    },
    "https://slu.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/Sinquefield-Science-and-Engineering-Center/Post-Doctoral-Fellow_2026-10028": {
      "title": "Post Doctoral Fellow",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-08-26\nFull time\n\nWho is Saint Louis University? Founded in 1818, Saint Louis University is one of the nation’s oldest and most prestigious Catholic universities. SLU, which also has a campus in Madrid, Spain, is recognized for world-class academics, life-changing research, compassionate health care, and a strong commitment to faith and service. Postdoctoral Research Fellow: AI, XR, & Human-Centric Simulation We are seeking a highly motivated Postdoctoral Research Fellow to lead innovative projects at the intersection of Modern AI , Computer Graphics , and VR/AR/XRd Human-Computer Interaction . This role focuses on utilizing VR/AR as a medium for behavioral transformation—specifically in high-fidelity motor skill acquisition and the enhancement of social communication. Primary Research Projects The successful candidate will contribute to and lead research in the following areas related to our current and past projects https://gxrlab.rf.gd/research/ : Intelligent Motor Skill Learning: Developing AI-driven, physics-based simulations in VR/AR to facilitate the acquisition of complex physical tasks. This includes real-time feedback loops, biomechanical modeling, and adaptive training environments. Social & Soft Skill Enhancement: Designing immersive social settings that leverage AI to improve interpersonal communication. Projects focus on creating responsive virtual agents and evaluative frameworks for social interaction. Key Responsibilities Research & Development: Integrate Physics-Informed Neural Networks or Reinforcement Learning to create realistic human movement and interactive social behaviors within XR. Instructional Leadership: Assist in teaching and curriculum development for undergraduate and graduate courses in Computer Graphics and Virtual Reality . This includes helping instructions, designing lab assignments, and mentoring students on technical projects. System Design: Build and maintain immersive prototypes that combine real-time physics with modern AI models to support learning and communication. Academic Leadership: Lead the submission of research to high-impact venues such as SIGGRAPH , IEEE VR , and CHI . Student Mentorship: Co-supervise Ph.D. and undergraduate researchers, fostering a collaborative and inclusive laboratory environment. Required Qualifications Ph.D. in Computer Science, Robotics, HCI, or a related field. Function Research Support Scheduled Weekly Hours: 40 Saint Louis University is an equal opportunity/affirmative action employer. All qualified candidates will receive consideration for the position applied for without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, disability, marital status, sexual orientation, military/veteran status, gender identity, or other non-merit factors. If accommodations are needed for completing the application and/or with the interviewing process, please contact Human Resources at 314-977-5847."
    },
